## Hint 1

`useSyncExternalStore` re-renders when the value returned by its `getSnapshot`
argument changes by `Object.is`. So the question "should a rename re-render the
card count" is really "does the function I pass return a different value after a
rename". Choose what that function returns.

## Hint 2

The hook's contract, in miniature — a component that follows the network status:

```tsx
const online = useSyncExternalStore(
  (listener) => {
    window.addEventListener("online", listener);
    window.addEventListener("offline", listener);
    return () => {
      window.removeEventListener("online", listener);
      window.removeEventListener("offline", listener);
    };
  },
  () => navigator.onLine,
);
```

`subscribe` takes React's listener and returns the teardown; `getSnapshot`
returns a value React can compare.

## Hint 3

Have `useBoardSlice` call `useSyncExternalStore(store.subscribe, () =>
selector(store.getSnapshot()))`, and have `CardCount` select
`state.cards.length` — a number, so a rename changes nothing. Inside the store,
keep the state in one object and replace it on every write with `{ ...state,
cards: [...state.cards, text] }`. The decision left to you is whether
`subscribe` should be a bound method or an arrow stored on the object: React
re-subscribes whenever the `subscribe` function's identity changes, so it must
be stable across renders.

