## Exercise 1 — the exhaustive switch

Edit `ex1/solution.tsx`. Export the action type, the reducer and the component.

```ts
type Item = { id: string; name: string; quantity: number };
type CartState = { items: Item[] };

export type CartAction =
  | { type: "added"; item: Item }
  | { type: "removed"; id: string }
  | { type: "quantityChanged"; id: string; quantity: number }
  | { type: "cleared" };

export function cartReducer(state: CartState, action: CartAction): CartState;
```

`CartPanel({ catalogue })` renders one button per catalogue entry reading
`Add <name>`, a `role="status"` paragraph reading `Lines: <n> · Units: <m>`, a
`Clear` button, and one row per item with the name, the quantity, and a button
reading `Remove <name>`.

Requirements:

- `quantityChanged` with a quantity of `0` or less removes the line;
- the default branch assigns `action` to a `const impossible: never` and throws;
- the reducer never mutates `state` or any item in it;
- `Clear` on an already-empty cart returns the **same** state object.

